---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { tide } from '../lib/tide';

const flakeSnippet = `{
  inputs.shady.url = "github:gloaming-dusk/shady";

  outputs = { nixpkgs, shady, ... }: {
    nixosConfigurations.my-machine = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
      system = "x86_64-linux";
      modules = [
        ./configuration.nix
        shady.nixosModules.default
        {
          programs.shady.enable = true;
          programs.shady.rice = "horizon";
          programs.shady.greeter.enable = true;
        }
      ];
    };
  };
}`;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Getting started · Shady"
  description="Build and run Shady and shady-shell nested, in safe mode, from a Linux VT, or as a NixOS login session."
  path="/getting-started/"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p>
      <h1>Run Shady without guessing.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Try it in a window with one command. To build it yourself, start nested,
        verify the compatibility path, then move to native DRM/libinput when you
        are ready. The <a href="/docs/getting-started/">full guide</a> also covers
        the keys and your own configuration.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="page-content">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell two-col">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">One command</p>
          <h2>Try it in a window.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            From any Wayland desktop with Nix, this builds Shady and opens Horizon
            inside a window, with a terminal. Press <code>Super+Shift+/</code> to see
            every shortcut of the session.
          </p>
          <p><code>SHADY_RICE=objects</code> in front picks another rice. Run from a text console, it starts full screen.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-window">
          <div class="code-title">nix run</div>
          <pre><code>nix run github:gloaming-dusk/shady
SHADY_RICE=objects nix run github:gloaming-dusk/shady</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="shell two-col">
      <div class="steps">
        <article class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Enter the development shell</h3>
            <p>Shady targets wlroots 0.20.2. The Nix shell supplies Meson, Ninja, Wayland tooling, Lua, GLES/EGL, and the test utilities.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Build the compositor</h3>
            <p><code>./tools/build.sh</code> creates or reconfigures the Meson build and runs Ninja.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Run nested first</h3>
            <p>Use the Wayland backend inside your current compositor. This is the easiest place to validate clients and configuration.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Try the compatibility path</h3>
            <p><code>--safe</code> bypasses the spatial renderer, physics, FPS interaction, and visual effects.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Move to a real VT</h3>
            <p>Once nested operation is reliable, use <code>./tools/run-native.sh</code> for DRM + libinput on a normal Linux VT login.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <div>
            <h3>Pick a rice</h3>
            <p>A rice starts the compositor with <code>shady-shell</code> and a terminal. Start with <a href="/demo/horizon/">Horizon</a>, the default (<code>./rices/horizon/run.sh</code>), then try Objects, <a href="/demo/afterglow/">Afterglow</a> or Neon Transit, or read one as a template for your own config.{tide && <> To live in, <a href="/demo/tide/">Tide</a> tiles windows in scrolling columns with niri's keys (<code>./rices/tide/run.sh</code>).</>}</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="stack">
        <div class="code-window">
          <div class="code-title">build + nested run</div>
          <pre><code>nix develop
./tools/build.sh

WLR_BACKENDS=wayland ./build/shady -s foot</code></pre>
        </div>


        <div class="code-window">
          <div class="code-title">safe compatibility path</div>
          <pre><code>WLR_BACKENDS=wayland ./build/shady --safe

# First native smoke test from a real VT
./tools/run-native.sh --safe -s foot</code></pre>
        </div>


        <aside class="notice">
          Shady is still experimental. Treat nested mode and <code>--safe</code> as
          recovery-friendly baselines before relying on a full spatial native session.
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell two-col">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">NixOS</p>
          <h2>Install it as a login session.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            The flake's NixOS module adds a Shady session to any NixOS system:
            the compositor, shady-shell, the rices and, if you like, the Shady
            greeter for greetd.
          </p>
          <p><code>programs.shady.rice</code> picks the rice used for whatever you have not configured in <code>~/.config/shady/</code>: <code>horizon</code>, <code>objects</code>, <code>afterglow</code>{tide ? <>, <code>neon-transit</code> or <code>tide</code></> : <> or <code>neon-transit</code></>}. See the <a href="/docs/greeter/">greeter docs</a> for the login screen{tide && <>; <code>programs.shady.greeter.theme = "tide"</code> gives it Tide's look</>}.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-window">
          <div class="code-title">flake.nix</div>
          <pre><code>{flakeSnippet}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell two-col">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Regression gates</p>
          <h2>Fast checks before you trust a build.</h2>
          <p class="lede">The repository includes separate core and spatial gates for quick local validation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-window">
          <div class="code-title">stability checks</div>
          <pre><code>./tools/daily-driver.sh all
./tools/spatial-daily-driver.sh all
./tests/spatial-suite.sh</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
